// pfodWeb NOTE: per-board override — this is the Fri3d Camp 2024 badge.
// Removed from the chip-level default chipGpios map:
//  4,5    TFT_DC/TFT_CS (onboard ST7789 display)
//  6,7,8,14  shared TFT+SD SPI bus (MOSI/SCK/MISO/SS)
//  10,11  IR blaster/receiver (fixed onboard IR hardware)
//  15,17  I2S mic on the communicator add-on
//  42     PIN_AUX, the badge's auxiliary power-rail control line
// (GPIO19/20, native USB D-/D+, are already excluded chip-wide.)
// Kept as general-purpose: joystick X/Y (1,3), buttons A/B/X/Y/MENU/
// START (39,40,38,41,45,0), buzzer (46), battery monitor (13),
// WS2812 LED (12), and general I2C (9,18).
// Full copy of variants/esp32/esp32s3/board.json otherwise.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO0, GPIO38, GPIO39, GPIO40, GPIO41, GPIO45 tagged
// "button" - confirmed by Fri3dCamp's official ESPHome doc
// (fri3dcamp.github.io/badge_2024/esphome/) which lists binary_sensor
// entries for START/X/A/B/Y/MENU on these pins, all pullup:true
// inverted:true, matching pins_arduino.h PIN_START/X/A/B/Y/MENU.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO12 tagged "led_neopixel" - confirmed by the same
// ESPHome doc (light platform: neopixelbus, type GRB, variant WS2812,
// pin GPIO12, num_leds:5), matching pins_arduino.h PIN_WS2812.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO21 tagged "led_high" - confirmed by the same ESPHome
// doc (light platform: status_led, pin GPIO21, no "inverted" field =>
// ESPHome default false = HIGH-is-on), matching pins_arduino.h
// LED_BUILTIN/PIN_LED.
{
  "boardName": "ESP32S3",
  "displayName": "ESP32-S3 Dev Module",
  "family": "esp32",
  "pwm": {
    "min": 0,
    "max": 255,
    "method": "analogWrite"
  },
  "dac": {},
